From 183659f10884864b833f35049c52cd5bf042358e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:57:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: samsung: s1402x: flush the data path when the stream
 stops

Nothing empties the mixer FIFO when playback ends, so the last period
keeps being replayed for as long as the codec stays powered.  What is
heard is that fragment on loop at the period rate: a periodic whine,
high pitched and unrelated to the frequency or the amplitude of the
material that was playing.  It lasts six to seven seconds, until DAPM
finally powers the DAC down.

Measured on gtaxlwifi (SM-T580).  Three observations agree:

  - a file padded with a second of silence produces no tail at all,
    which is what replaying a stale buffer of silence sounds like;
  - toggling DATA_RSTB by hand during the tail cuts it instantly;
  - PWR_DIG_1 reads 0x8c80 throughout, so I2S1 and both DAC channels
    are still converting: this is real audio, not an amplifier
    oscillating without its reference.

The reset already exists and its comment upstream says exactly this,
that it flushes the existing data buffer; it was simply never called
on the way out.  Doing it from shutdown() keeps it in process context,
unlike trigger(), and the mixer is idle by then anyway.
---
 sound/soc/samsung/s1402x.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/samsung/s1402x.c b/sound/soc/samsung/s1402x.c
index 9b70a67704..de6f661f5e 100644
--- a/sound/soc/samsung/s1402x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/s1402x.c
@@ -285,9 +285,25 @@ static int s1402x_set_bclk_ratio(struct snd_soc_dai *dai, unsigned int ratio)
 				  xfs << INCTL2_I2S_XFS_SHIFT);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The mixer keeps replaying its last buffer once the stream stops, so
+ * the final period is heard on loop for as long as the codec stays
+ * powered - several seconds, as a periodic whine that has nothing to
+ * do with the material that was playing.  Flush the data path on
+ * close, which is what the reset is documented to be for.
+ */
+static void s1402x_shutdown(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
+			    struct snd_soc_dai *dai)
+{
+	struct s1402x_priv *priv = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(dai->component);
+
+	s1402x_reset_data(priv);
+}
+
 static const struct snd_soc_dai_ops s1402x_dai_ops = {
 	.hw_params	= s1402x_hw_params,
 	.set_bclk_ratio	= s1402x_set_bclk_ratio,
+	.shutdown	= s1402x_shutdown,
 };
 
 static struct snd_soc_dai_driver s1402x_dais[] = {
